The mismatches are because of my *test's* escaping: the non-expression path uses `''.join('\\x%02x'%c if c>126 or c<32 else chr(c) for c in blob)` — in a JSON *string* template (not an expression), `\x41` is literal backslash-x-4-1 characters, not an escape! So the bytes differ. That's my test bug: for the literal path I must only use characters that survive JSON→UTF-8 encoding, i.e. bytes < 128 mapped via chr(), and bytes > 127 can't be represented literally.

