Note: the literal form must also be careful with `"` and `\` characters inside the blob (they'd need JSON escaping — json.dumps handles that ✓ since I pass a Python str and json.dumps escapes it properly ✓). And the resulting template string, when encoded to UTF-8, gives exactly the original bytes for bytes < 128 ✓.

