insert(long off, byte[] data, List<Undo> journal):
- if data.length == 0 → return true.
- end = off + len (caller guarantees no overflow).
- Collect overlapping segments: start from floorEntry(off); iterate while entry != null && entry.value.start < end.
  Actually floorEntry(off) gives the segment with the greatest start ≤ off; it may or may not overlap (if its end <= off, no overlap).
- Pass 1: verify equality for all overlaps. If any mismatch → return false.
- Pass 2: mutate:
  - removed = list of segments fully/partially overlapped that we remove.
  - added = list of new segments.
  For each overlapping seg S:
    - remove S from map, add to removed.
    - if S.start < off: add Seg(S.start, off, copy of S.data[0..off-S.start])
    - if S.end > end: add Seg(end, S.end, copy of S.data[end-S.start .. S.end-S.start])
  - add Seg(off, end, data)
  - put all new segs into the map, record in added.
  - journal.push(() -> { for (Seg a : added) map.remove(a.start); for (Seg r : removed) map.put(r.start, r); });

