Let me try to construct a case that defeats the bound. The bound is: min over active nodes n of (top-avail_n benefits through n + suffix - throughSum_n). This is strong when nodes are shared. The weakest case: items that share few nodes... but then components split.

Let me think about when the bound is weak: a single binding node n with avail = c and many items through it → the bound = sum of top-c benefits, which is exactly achievable → tight. Multiple nodes → tighter. So the bound is essentially always strong.

