Let me optimize the brute force: precompute for each predicate a frozenset of universe indices where true, and a frozenset of train indices where true. Then:
- clause covers train iff union of train sets == all train indices.
- minimal iff for each i, union of others != all.
- counterexample: universe falsifying = complement of union of universe sets → smallest index.
- witnesses: for literal i, smallest train index in (train_set[i] - union of others).
- queries: iterate over universe windows (still needed for fixed/prefix/clauses) — can precompute per-clause universe sets and per-cell value index sets.

